szcompressor/SZ3 v3.4.0, revision 592df793eb596d952242aa9fec9cbe5e68782aae.
https://github.com/szcompressor/SZ3

include/SZ3 holds only the headers of the 2D interpolation pipeline (SZGenericCompressor,
InterpolationDecomposition, LinearQuantizer, HuffmanEncoder and Lossless_bypass) and what they
include, with the local decoder changes below. The public SZ_compress API, the other algorithms and Lossless_zstd are
left out: they require zstd. version.hpp is upstream version.hpp.in configured for 3.4.0.

The TWM raster profile (libs/indexer/terrain/sz3_profile.hpp) composes these modules directly
into a headerless frame and replaces the zstd stage with optional deflate. Like SPERR, the
reconstructed integer heights must match on all supported architectures: the encoder and the
decoder are built with strict floating point.

Local decoder changes retain the Huffman table and bin storage, use direct 2D block traversal and
integer interpolator dispatch, and compute the grid levels with integer bit widths. The stream
layout and the reconstruction order are unchanged. On GCC/Clang, CMakeLists.txt defines
SZ3_ASSUME_STRICT_FP: every source including SZ3 must then use -fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off.
This removes the volatile spills of nofma() in def.hpp without permitting FMA or reassociation,
and fast-math builds with that definition are rejected. Other builds (the Xcode projects) keep
the volatile barriers.
